// The spent-voucher record in the directory (DESIGN §9, F5), and what deleting
// a host does to it.
//
// A voucher carries a salt. kuipad accepts a salt once: it refuses a join whose
// salt is already recorded as spent. `Slot(salt, 'fresh')` is the absence of such a
// record and `Slot(salt, 'spent')` its presence: one token per salt that a join
// moves from fresh to spent, a rollback moves back, and a purge removes. `Alive(salt)` is the
// voucher's validity window: the signature verifies until its expiry.
//
// Previous code kept the record on the host entry (ipaKUVoucherSpent), so deleting
// the host freed the salt; peer-voucher-spent-previous.spthy models that and the
// other previous behaviour as controls.
//
// Current code writes one record per salt (ipaKUVoucherSpentRecord) that
// outlives the host: `host_delete` removes the host entry only. A purge removes
// a record once the voucher can no longer verify (`expire`, then `purge`), so
// the directory does not grow without bound.
//
// A join is `join_add` (record and host entry written; the join is `Pending`),
// then `group_ok`, or a failure. A failed join keeps the record unless the host
// is certainly absent: `group_fails_rollback` (the host delete succeeded)
// releases the salt; a lost reply from the host add, or a host delete that fails
// (`group_fails_host_remains`), keep it. A refused host add leaves nothing to
// model. The salt is one token `Slot(salt, status)`, fresh or spent.
//
// Omitted: the signature and the join's key exchange (kuipa.spthy VoucherSingleUse
// owns those), the lease, the voucher's validity check at the join, and
// concurrent joins: the model has one directory, and two replicas that take the
// same salt before the record replicates are not covered.
//
// Run 2026-11-13, Tamarin 1.12.0, Maude 3.5.1, proofs.sh -t 300 (8 GiB), one lemma
// per process.
// Verified: join_then_delete, purge_after_join, rollback_then_retry,
// host_remains_reachable (reachability); second_host_needs_rollback;
// salt_single_use (uses second_host_needs_rollback as a source, [reuse], which
// verifies on its own); purge_only_after_expiry.
// Open: none.
theory peer_voucher_spent
begin

rule issue:
  [ Fr(~salt) ]
  --[ Issued(~salt) ]->
  [ Slot(~salt, 'fresh'), Alive(~salt) ]

// A join writes the spent record, then the host entry, then adds the host to
// its group (kuipad's join in directory.rs). `Pending` is the join between the
// host add and the group update.
rule join_add:
  [ Slot(salt, 'fresh'), Fr(~host) ]
  --[ HostCreated(salt, ~host) ]->
  [ Slot(salt, 'spent'), Host(~host, salt), Pending(~host, salt) ]

// The group update succeeds and the join is done.
rule group_ok:
  [ Pending(host, salt) ]
  --[ Joined(salt, host) ]->
  [ ]

// The group update fails and the host delete succeeds: the voucher enrolled
// no one and the record is released, so a retry can work.
rule group_fails_rollback:
  [ Pending(host, salt), Host(host, salt), Slot(salt, 'spent') ]
  --[ RolledBack(salt, host) ]->
  [ Slot(salt, 'fresh') ]

// The group update fails and the host delete fails too, or the host add
// committed but reported an error: a host may exist. Current code keeps the
// record.
rule group_fails_host_remains:
  [ Pending(host, salt) ]
  --[ HostRemains(salt, host) ]->
  [ ]

// Current code: the host goes, the record stays.
rule host_delete:
  [ Host(host, salt) ]
  --[ HostDeleted(host, salt) ]->
  [ ]

// The window closes. An unused voucher lapses with it; a spent one leaves its
// record waiting to be purged.
rule expire:
  [ Alive(salt) ]
  --[ Expired(salt) ]->
  [ Closed(salt) ]

rule lapse:
  [ Closed(salt), Slot(salt, 'fresh') ]
  --[ Lapsed(salt) ]->
  [ ]

rule purge:
  [ Closed(salt), Slot(salt, 'spent') ]
  --[ Purged(salt) ]->
  [ ]

// Reachability: a voucher enrols a host that is then deleted; a failed group
// update rolls back and the salt is used again.
lemma join_then_delete: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i #j. Joined(salt, host) @i & HostDeleted(host, salt) @j & #i < #j"
lemma purge_after_join: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i #j. Joined(salt, host) @i & Purged(salt) @j & #i < #j"
lemma rollback_then_retry: exists-trace
  "Ex salt h1 h2 #i #j #k. HostCreated(salt, h1) @i & RolledBack(salt, h1) @j & HostCreated(salt, h2) @k & #j < #k & not(h1 = h2)"
lemma host_remains_reachable: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i. HostRemains(salt, host) @i"

// A second host is created for a salt only after the first was cleanly rolled
// back; a lost reply, a failed delete or an administrator's host-del never makes
// the salt usable again.
lemma second_host_needs_rollback [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All salt h1 h2 #i #j. HostCreated(salt, h1) @i & HostCreated(salt, h2) @j & #i < #j
     ==> Ex #k. RolledBack(salt, h1) @k & #i < #k & #k < #j"

// A salt completes a join at most once, whatever happens to the host in between.
// A corollary of the lemma above, which it uses as a source: the first host's
// rollback consumes the join before it can complete.
lemma salt_single_use:
  "All salt h1 h2 #i #j. Joined(salt, h1) @i & Joined(salt, h2) @j ==> #i = #j"

// A record is purged only after the voucher's window closed, so a purge never
// makes a still-valid voucher usable again.
lemma purge_only_after_expiry:
  "All salt #i. Purged(salt) @i ==> Ex #j. Expired(salt) @j & #j < #i"
end
